# The page's own headers, against injected scripts, framing, content sniffing and referrer leaks.
# Two content security policies (server:csp-reports-to-own-origin). The first is enforced: the browser refuses what it
# does not allow. The second only reports: it is the first made stricter, and says what it would refuse before it is
# safe to enforce; once its reports are quiet, it takes the first's place.
# To roll the first back to reporting alone, add -Report-Only to its name; a browser then refuses nothing.
# Both report to the server's /api/csp-report: report-to names the Reporting API's endpoint, which Reporting-Endpoints
# defines on this origin, and report-uri is the older form for browsers without it. Both are paths on the page's own
# origin, so the same file serves every deployment.
# The enforced policy is a list of sources rather than nonces: the files are served as they are with no server to mint a
# nonce, and the two outside scripts (the bot check, the beacon) are not versioned, so no hash of them holds. 'self'
# serves only the build and the API's JSON, which nosniff keeps from ever running as script. The page's one inline
# script, the life's hint (vite/life-ahead.plugin.ts: preload links for a browser with a life, nothing else), is
# allowed by its sha256 hash alone, which the build writes in place of the token in braces in both policies' script-src;
# its file names change with every build, so its hash does too. No 'unsafe-inline' for scripts, in either policy.
# wasm-unsafe-eval: the models' mesh decoder, WebAssembly only; no string ever runs as script ('unsafe-eval' is never
# allowed, and public/zod-jitless.js keeps Zod from trying). challenges.cloudflare.com: the bot check's script and frame.
# blob: the models' textures, fetched from blob addresses, their decoder's worker, and the shared cards.
# font-src data: the sign font, small enough that the build inlines it.
# style-src 'unsafe-inline' while the stricter policy reports: the splash and the legal pages carry inline styles.
# form-action 'none': every form of the game is handled in code and never submits; signing in is a fetch and a move to
# Google's page, not a form. manifest-src and every other kind fall back to default-src 'self'.
# No upgrade-insecure-requests: every address the page uses is its own or https already, so it would change nothing in
# production and would break the local preview over http.
# If the server is ever on another address than the page, connect-src names it, with its wss: form.
# static.cloudflareinsights.com and cloudflareinsights.com: Cloudflare Web Analytics' beacon and its reports,
# in the page only when the build has VITE_ANALYTICS_TOKEN (vite/analytics.plugin.ts).
# The stricter policy: Trusted Types, so a script's address is only ever set through the page's one policy, japacity
# (shared/policy/trusted.ts); and inline styles only by their hashes, which the build writes in place of the token in
# braces (vite/style-hashes.plugin.ts), with no style attribute (the game's own styles are set in code, which no
# policy governs).
# Caching (server:production-and-staging): every file is asked about again before use (no-cache: kept, but
# revalidated), so a new build reaches the next load; the page itself above all. Only the files under /assets/ whose
# names carry the hash of their contents (the build's code, the models) are kept for a year untouched. The models'
# manifest has a fixed name, so it is asked about every time like the page. A later rule's "! Cache-Control" drops
# the earlier rule's value, so each path carries one.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'wasm-unsafe-eval' https://challenges.cloudflare.com https://static.cloudflareinsights.com {inline-script-hashes}; frame-src https://challenges.cloudflare.com; connect-src 'self' blob: https://cloudflareinsights.com; img-src 'self' data: blob:; media-src 'self' blob:; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; worker-src 'self' blob:; font-src 'self' data:; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; report-uri /api/csp-report; report-to csp
  Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'wasm-unsafe-eval' https://challenges.cloudflare.com https://static.cloudflareinsights.com {inline-script-hashes}; frame-src https://challenges.cloudflare.com; connect-src 'self' blob: https://cloudflareinsights.com; img-src 'self' data: blob:; media-src 'self' blob:; style-src 'self' {inline-style-hashes}; style-src-attr 'none'; worker-src 'self' blob:; font-src 'self' data:; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; require-trusted-types-for 'script'; trusted-types japacity; report-uri /api/csp-report; report-to csp
  Reporting-Endpoints: csp="/api/csp-report"
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/index.html
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/assets/*
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/assets/manifest.json
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: no-cache
